WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.120
 Write as though nobody's
watching because nobody's

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.010
watching.

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:08.620
Suspense is all about making
promises to your reader.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:11.520
You're telling your reader, I
know something you don't know,

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:13.610
but I promise I'll tell
you if you keep going.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:18.410
Writing a novel is
about a process.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:21.640
It is not all about
inspiration and craft.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.340
This class provides
practical tools,

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:29.010
a roadmap to turn your
idea into a story.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:31.080
Take the pressure off yourself.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.920
Every single idea has
been done over and over.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:35.544
You don't need a big idea.

00:00:35.544 --> 00:00:38.830
You need big how's.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:40.370
How do you create tension?

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:41.500
How do you build character?

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.140
What's the moral gray area that
we're going to be writing in?

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:47.350
There are elements that
must be in a good story--

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:50.020
the contract, the
clock, and the crucible.

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:54.540
If you're not sure
what to write,

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:56.650
write the wrong
thing a few times

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:59.830
and let that be the process by
which you find the right thing.

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:02.740
Put a secret in a
character's back story.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:05.890
Write your villain first because
your villain is the one who's

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.230
going to define your hero.

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:10.750
There were some dark times
when I wasn't actually sure

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:12.250
I could accomplish this.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:15.640
There will be days you just
don't know if you can do it.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:20.530
And on those days, what is going
to save you is your process.

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:23.920
You do not need to have total
mastery of your subject matter

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.050
to start a novel,
only to finish it.

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:30.190
Write until you're ready to
show the world what you've done.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:34.500
I'm Dan Brown, and
this is my MasterClass.

